<Base title={title} description={description}><Fragment slot="head"><script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}/><script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-HXM22WWPKP"></script><script is:inline>window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments)}gtag('js',new Date());gtag('config','G-HXM22WWPKP');</script></Fragment>
<section class="hero" id="top"><img class="hero-image" src="/images/pearl-2025-1600.jpg" srcset="/images/pearl-2025-800.jpg 800w, /images/pearl-2025-1600.jpg 1600w" sizes="100vw" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Pearl Street storefronts and pedestrian paving, photographed in December 2025" fetchpriority="high"/><div class="hero-shade"></div><div class="container hero-copy"><p class="hero-kicker">Four pedestrian blocks · Boulder, Colorado</p><h1>Pearl<br/>Street Mall</h1><p class="hero-lead">Explore the outdoor pedestrian blocks between 11th and 15th Streets, with separate shops, dining and civic spaces along the way. Check the day’s access and the businesses you plan to visit.</p><p class="rating">Google Maps 4.6/5 · 10,677 reviews</p><p class="snapshot">Manual snapshot checked 2026-10-30. It does not update automatically and is not a set of reviews collected by this guide.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#plan">Plan the visit</a><a class="button outline" href={MAPS} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check the place on Maps ↗</a></div></div></section>
<div class="photo-credit container">Historical photograph: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pearl_Street_Mall_(55028393862).jpg">Jesse James / Wikimedia Commons</a>,17 December 2025, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Cropped, resized and recompressed; social image additionally cropped. It does not show today’s conditions, available entrances or a current tenant inventory.</div>
<section id="about" class="section brick-grid"><div class="container two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">An outdoor city place</p><h2 class="section-title">Four blocks within downtown</h2><p>Pearl Street Mall is an outdoor pedestrian street and city park. The <a href="https://bouldercolorado.gov/projects/pearl-street-mall-refresh">City identifies its core as 11th to 15th Street</a>; Pearl Street and downtown continue beyond it. Use normal crossings at the intersecting streets.</p><p>The City records dedication as a public park on 6 August 1977. Its brick paving and gathering spaces developed through an effort to orient this part of downtown toward pedestrians. The City’s June 2026 project update describes assessment and preparation for 2027 maintenance and anniversary work. Check the <a href="https://bouldercolorado.gov/projects/pearl-street-mall-refresh">refresh project</a> for changes affecting your visit; this guide has no live works monitoring.</p></div><aside class="card text-card"><h3>Location reference</h3><p><strong>Maps lists 1303 Pearl St, Boulder, CO 80302.</strong> Downtown Boulder identifies the Visitor Information Center at that address, near 13th Street. It is not a single entrance or a street number covering every business.</p><p>The City’s park page lists accessible paths, benches and drinking fountains. Maps also marked an accessible entrance on{' '}{REVIEW_DATE}; neither is a full survey of crossings, grades, temporary barriers or individual businesses.</p></aside></div></section>
<section id="plan" class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Plan the day</p><h2 class="section-title">Hours, access and parking</h2><div class="three-col"><article class="card text-card"><h3>Street and business hours</h3><p>Maps listed 24 hours on{' '}{REVIEW_DATE}. This is a dated third-party listing, not confirmation of live access, lighting or night-time safety. Downtown Boulder says stores are independently operated and hours vary; visitor services and events also have their own schedules.</p></article><article class="card text-card"><h3>Fees and timing</h3><p>This review found no current general-admission tariff for the public pedestrian space. Budget separately for shopping, food, parking or ticketed programmes. Choose how long to stay around the venues and crossings you need; no fixed journey time is promised.</p></article><article class="card text-card"><h3>Facilities and rules</h3><p>Downtown Boulder lists public restrooms north of the visitor centre at 13th and Pearl and another location at 9th and Canyon. Confirm current access and facilities. Read the <a href="https://boulderdowntown.com/about/boulder-faqs/rules-for-the-mall">published mall rules</a> on animals, service-animal provisions, cycling, skating and smoking; dismount bicycles on the bricks.</p></article></div><div class="two-col space-top"><article class="card text-card"><h3>Choose an actual garage</h3><p>The <a href="https://bouldercolorado.gov/services/city-parking-garages">City directory</a> lists garages at 10th and Walnut, 11th and Walnut, 11th and Spruce, 14th and Walnut, and 15th and Pearl. It also warns of ongoing 2026 repair work. The City’s <a href="https://bouldercolorado.gov/news/city-manager-releases-balanced-budget-focus-critically-vital-services-and-community-input">28 August 2026 announcement of its 2027 Recommended Budget</a> also lists renovations to the 1500 Pearl Parking Garage. This is a budget recommendation, not confirmation of approval, a closure, construction dates or visitor impact; confirm those details with the City. A directory entry is not live confirmation of availability: check the construction notices and the exact facility before setting out.</p><p>The City publishes free weekend and city-holiday parking in its downtown garages, with exceptions and separate terms elsewhere. Do not transfer that arrangement to every private garage, street space or Depot Square Boulder Junction. Check posted rates, service fees and payment instructions for your chosen facility.</p></article><article class="card text-card"><h3>Transit and the outdoor plan</h3><p>The City identifies its 14th and Walnut garage beside the RTD bus station. Use <a href="https://www.rtd-denver.com/">RTD’s current journey information</a> to choose a service; this guide does not promise a particular frequency or walking time from every stop.</p><p>Plan shade, clothing and rest stops for the actual conditions. Check <a href="https://www.weather.gov/bou/">National Weather Service Boulder</a> forecasts and warnings before outdoor plans. The site has no live weather feed. Need a step-free route or specific facilities? Confirm the relevant entrance and crossing before arrival.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="eat" class="section pine"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow light">Food along and beyond the bricks</p><h2 class="section-title">Check the correct business</h2><p>These existing guide entries were checked against the operator or Downtown Boulder directory on{' '}{REVIEW_DATE}. They are separate businesses with their own prices, meal periods, reservations and access arrangements; no tasting, partnership or immediate table availability is claimed.</p><div class="three-col">{restaurants.map(item=><article class="restaurant-card text-card"><h3>{item.name}</h3><p><strong>{item.address}</strong></p><p>{item.description}</p><a href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Operator information ↗</a>{item.directory&&<p><a href={item.directory} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Downtown Boulder address listing ↗</a></p>}</article>)}</div><p>For a different venue or dietary need, use the <a href="https://boulderdowntown.com/dining">Downtown Boulder dining directory</a> and ask the business directly.</p></div></section>
<section id="nearby" class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">A separate destination</p><h2 class="section-title">Add a stop that fits</h2><p>The following places retain their own access, fees, conditions and schedules. They are not a surveyed short-walk circle or a guaranteed all-sights itinerary.</p><div class="three-col">{nearby.map(item=><article class="card text-card"><h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.body}</p><a href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official visitor information ↗</a></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section id="reviews" class="section sand"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Place and review reference</p><h2 class="section-title">A dated Google Maps snapshot</h2><p><strong>4.6/5 · 10,677 reviews</strong>, manually checked on{' '}{REVIEW_DATE}. These figures do not update automatically, are not collected by this site and do not reproduce individual reviews.</p><p>Maps lists 1303 Pearl Street. Use it to orient yourself, then choose the actual open entrance or business you need. An area marker does not establish a surveyed accessible route.</p><a class="button" href={MAPS} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the place and current reviews ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="faq" class="section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Before you go</p><h2 class="section-title">Common questions</h2><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
<section id="sources" class="section sources"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Reviewed{' '}{REVIEW_DATE}</p><h2 class="section-title">Sources and image attribution</h2><ul>{sources.map(([href,label])=><li><a href={href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{label} ↗</a></li>)}</ul><p>Each source covers its own place and service. Event dates, commercial hours, parking and restrictions can change: follow current official and on-site notices. The event calendar is a planning link, not evidence that a programme is running today.</p><p>The delivered historical photograph is <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pearl_Street_Mall_(55028393862).jpg">Pearl Street Mall (55028393862).jpg</a>, Jesse James,17 December 2025, licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Local derivatives are cropped, resized and recompressed; the social version has an additional crop. No endorsement is implied. The photography licence does not independently clear every depicted person, sign, building or other subject right.</p></div></section>
<section id="privacy" class="section"><div class="container narrow"><h2 class="section-title">Privacy and use of this guide</h2><h3>Automatic Google Analytics</h3><p>The home page automatically loads Google Analytics 4 using the existing measurement identifier; it does not wait for a site consent switch. Google may use cookies and receive page URLs, referrers, browsing events, browser and device information. Complete anonymity is not promised. This site has no analytics consent or disable control; browser settings and <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google’s opt-out tool</a> may restrict some collection. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>.</p><h3>Hosting and independent measurement</h3><p>Cloudflare hosts this site and separately processes IP, connection, request, security and performance data. Two pre-update homepage HTML samples (apex and www, via Cloudflare LAX) fetched on{' '}{REVIEW_DATE} did not show an Insights beacon marker. Those samples do not establish absence in other responses or later settings. Hosting may independently provide visit measurement involving page views, URLs, referrers, browser, device and performance data. This is distinct from edge security processing and is not governed by a site GA switch. A marker alone would not prove script execution or successful transmission. See <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics documentation</a> and its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.</p><h3>Resources and limits</h3><p>Images load from this site. Maps, venue and official-source links lead to third parties with their own policies; this site does not request your location. An older version could cache pages offline. That cache is retired when the browser receives the updated worker; current information is not promised offline. This does not erase third-party cookies. There are no accounts, reviews submission, booking, payment or contact forms here.</p><p>This independent, unofficial, nonprofit tourism and educational guide provides dated planning information. It does not represent operators or promise real-time availability, safety, accessibility or a particular travel outcome. Check the current source and local conditions.</p></div></section>
